1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:09,030
So? According to Nanase,
you want my class's help.

2
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:11,000
Not quite.

3
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:15,160
I told her I'm willing
to work with your class.

4
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:20,160
No hierarchy. An alliance of equals.

5
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:22,720
Gotcha.

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:27,170
So you're not gonna bring up the
fact that you're a year ahead of us.

7
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:32,170
Smart of you not to try
playing the senpai card.

8
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,700
I recognize that there are

9
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:39,540
a significant number of first-years who
don't care if their classmates struggle.

10
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:45,350
But moving forward, you'll inevitably
reach a point when you'll need their aid.

11
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:51,190
"So let's work together to
make sure no one fails"?

12
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:58,450
Okay to assume that you're
Class 2-D's leader?

13
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:00,950
You're free to see things that way.

14
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:04,990
Then as leader, I'll give you a warning.

15
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:12,550
I didn't come here to work with you
under your so-called "equality."

16
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:14,650
What are you hoping for, then?

17
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:18,470
Did you think I would
pay you private points?

18
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:21,860
Yeah. Damn straight you'll pay.

19
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,820
That's the only way this goes anywhere.

20
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:27,540
I'm afraid I must repeat myself.

21
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,410
My proposal is an alliance of equals.

22
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:35,430
It would be inappropriate for either
side to offer payment to the other.

23
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,820
In that case...

24
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:42,830
I guess I'll just be going, then.

25
00:01:54,550 --> 00:02:00,350
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

26
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:10,960
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

27
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:18,680
#4 To Whom the Blade Turns

28
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,220
Wait!

29
00:03:20,810 --> 00:03:25,940
Hosen-kun, I think you should listen
to what Horikita-senpai has to say.

30
00:03:26,350 --> 00:03:28,470
Don't see why I should bother.

31
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:30,540
I do.

32
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:34,470
At this rate, our class
will be unable to unify.

33
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:36,980
What are you, stupid?

34
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:41,590
There's not a damn thing I get
out of agreeing to her offer.

35
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:46,240
I don't think your strategy is a bad one—

36
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,500
intentionally staying neutral and
passing on early negotiations

37
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:52,250
to give us a better negotiating position.

38
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Tell me one thing I get out
of working with Horikita here.

39
00:03:57,530 --> 00:03:59,510
Trust.

40
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:01,990
Trust, huh?

41
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:06,510
Bunch of head-in-the-clouds
bullshit, if you ask me.

42
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:10,330
If you turn the second-years
against you now,

43
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:13,380
and a similar test comes up in the future,

44
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:19,020
we may end up unable to secure partners,
no matter how many points we offer.

45
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:23,780
You think I'm scared of
eating the penalty for that?

46
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:26,230
I'm sure the penalty itself
wouldn't be a problem.

47
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,910
But what if the partner you end
up with intentionally does poorly?

48
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,540
You wouldn't be able to avoid expulsion.

49
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:37,470
You think someone here has the balls
to get expelled to take me down?

50
00:04:37,790 --> 00:04:42,800
In this school, it seems there's a
system known as protection points.

51
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:46,050
Yes, they're a special kind
of point that allows you

52
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:47,910
to nullify expulsion a single time.

53
00:04:48,610 --> 00:04:51,920
If the partner you end up
with has a protection point,

54
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:56,060
they could excise you from the school
without any risk to themselves.

55
00:04:56,650 --> 00:05:02,190
Which means it's best to establish
trust now, while we can.

56
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:04,300
I get it.

57
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,040
You idiots rubbed a couple
brain cells together

58
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:08,030
to figure out a way to threaten me.

59
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,790
Sorry to ruin your sad excuse for a plan,

60
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:15,410
but I'm not doing anything as equals.

61
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,810
What do you expect to do, then?

62
00:05:18,330 --> 00:05:21,800
We won't change our perception
of our classes as equals.

63
00:05:22,020 --> 00:05:25,050
Yeah, you made that clear.

64
00:05:25,550 --> 00:05:31,060
But I don't think we'd
actually be equal at all.

65
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:36,810
If you're so sure, then for my reference,
what is it that you propose?

66
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:40,060
A million private points.

67
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:42,970
Hand it over to me as collateral.

68
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:50,420
If I need your help for something
later, I'll gladly pay it all back.

69
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:54,580
If "trust" is so important to you,

70
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:57,130
that's not such a big ask, is it?

71
00:05:58,270 --> 00:06:01,750
Hosen skillfully got
his offer on the table.

72
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:04,260
He's more than just a musclehead.

73
00:06:04,710 --> 00:06:09,010
Like Ryuen, he's capable
of rather devious scheming.

74
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:13,060
I acknowledge the logic of your proposal.

75
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:16,270
But I can't agree to those terms.

76
00:06:16,530 --> 00:06:20,040
Gotcha. Too bad.

77
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:23,570
I thought I'd be generous
and toss you a lifeline,

78
00:06:23,570 --> 00:06:25,850
but I guess we've hit a roadblock again.

79
00:06:26,930 --> 00:06:28,280
It appears so.

80
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:35,510
You son of a—

81
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:36,910
Don't do it, Sudo-kun!

82
00:06:37,410 --> 00:06:39,660
What do you expect me to do?!

83
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,820
If you're that upset about
reaching an impasse,

84
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:47,670
you should have come
up with a better idea.

85
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,150
Let's go.

86
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:51,700
You sure about this?!

87
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:57,060
Are you sure about this, Hosen-kun?

88
00:07:04,650 --> 00:07:06,190
Hold up.

89
00:07:06,930 --> 00:07:12,570
I won't change my position as long as you
insist on making unreasonable demands.

90
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,470
Fine, gotcha.

91
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:18,360
I'll order my class to pair up with yours.

92
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:20,780
So give me some points.

93
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:22,330
Two million.

94
00:07:23,050 --> 00:07:24,250
Two million?

95
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:26,590
You've shown your true colors.

96
00:07:26,590 --> 00:07:31,020
It's the only way for your
class to avoid expulsion.

97
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:34,340
You won't gain anything by cheaping out.

98
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:36,600
This is getting us nowhere.

99
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:42,500
Fine, fine. I'll consider your offer.

100
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,830
That's quite a sudden change of heart.

101
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:50,130
Why wouldn't I try to squeeze out
the best terms for myself first?

102
00:07:50,130 --> 00:07:54,490
Then you'll accept my terms
for an alliance of equals?

103
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:58,640
Yeah. Let's talk it out, no more violence.

104
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:01,450
But people might see us here.

105
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:03,250
Let's go somewhere else.

106
00:08:03,610 --> 00:08:06,960
Very well. I'll give you ten minutes.

107
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,870
Gotcha. I'll show you to the spot.

108
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:16,780
Our offer on the table hasn't changed.

109
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:19,430
Yeah, so mine is...

110
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:21,430
Three million.

111
00:08:22,170 --> 00:08:27,810
Hand it straight to me, and I'll
save you dumb assholes right now.

112
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,810
You're screwing with us!

113
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,780
Nah, I'm dead serious.

114
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:37,320
I wouldn't have reopened
negotiations otherwise.

115
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:40,980
It was a mistake to even entertain this.

116
00:08:43,250 --> 00:08:44,330
Suzune!

117
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,830
What are you—

118
00:08:56,760 --> 00:09:00,510
Let's see how much fight
you've got in you.

119
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,350
You're on.

120
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:07,480
I won't hold back against an
asshole who'd hurt Suzune!

121
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:15,110
What... What do you think you're doing?!

122
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:16,860
Horikita-senpai.

123
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:21,830
I believe things at this school have
changed a bit from how they were before.

124
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:27,370
We first-years know the current
situation better than you do.

125
00:09:27,590 --> 00:09:28,880
What are you talking about?

126
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:32,580
A few representatives of
the first-years received

127
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:35,620
an explanation directly
from President Nagumo—

128
00:09:36,470 --> 00:09:40,680
that, this year, he was going to make
the school even more of a meritocracy.

129
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:42,390
That's ridiculous!

130
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,640
He's even allowing fights
between students?!

131
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:52,060
Hey, Sudo. Have a look
at Horikita over there.

132
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:55,670
She looks pretty damn pissed.

133
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:59,030
Y-You...

134
00:09:57,490 --> 00:10:01,010
He has far more real-life
fighting experience than Sudo.

135
00:10:01,770 --> 00:10:05,540
I see. That's why even Ryuen didn't
want to get physical with him.

136
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:14,330
So...

137
00:10:14,710 --> 00:10:16,720
You wanna go strength for strength?

138
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:19,970
Fighting like this isn't helping anyone!

139
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:35,230
Does Hosen really think he can gain
the upper hand through sheer violence?

140
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:40,110
No, I don't think he's that stupid.

141
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:43,290
Then by starting this fight...

142
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:47,350
What does Hosen hope to accomplish?

143
00:10:48,370 --> 00:10:54,880
Well, your big, strong bodyguard
is down for the count.

144
00:10:55,130 --> 00:10:59,250
Did you think you could break
our spirits with violence?

145
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:02,820
I'm gonna beat you down so hard,

146
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:06,530
you'll be begging me to
let you sign an agreement.

147
00:11:07,310 --> 00:11:10,770
Very well. Then I'll stop you myself.

148
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:12,950
Ain't that something?

149
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,270
If you wanna show me what you've got...

150
00:11:15,530 --> 00:11:18,210
I'll be happy to see it!

151
00:11:25,730 --> 00:11:29,520
Pretty nice moves, I gotta say!

152
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:32,750
S-Suzune!

153
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:40,020
Hey, Horikita.

154
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:42,510
Let's make an agreement.

155
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:44,530
You give me five million.

156
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:48,180
Then all of this ends.

157
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:50,680
Th-This is absurd.

158
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:54,810
Ayanokoji-kun, call the teachers!

159
00:11:54,810 --> 00:11:57,070
Wouldn't do that if I were you.

160
00:11:57,550 --> 00:12:03,820
Unless you want her
injuries to get way worse.

161
00:12:04,630 --> 00:12:07,510
Horikita, I'm giving you one last chance.

162
00:12:07,510 --> 00:12:11,640
Agree to my terms and get
me the points I want,

163
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:14,580
or I'll kill Ayanokoji.

164
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:17,340
What in the world are you...

165
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:24,090
If you don't agree, I'll skewer Ayanokoji.

166
00:12:24,090 --> 00:12:28,720
And that's on the light end of
things I'd do to get points.

167
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:30,840
That's enough!

168
00:12:31,290 --> 00:12:34,480
I've made up my mind!
I refuse to accept your methods!

169
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:38,230
Clear out, Nanase. I'm doing this.

170
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,730
I'm sorry, Horikita-senpai.

171
00:12:41,210 --> 00:12:44,410
You were never going to be able to
make an agreement with Hosen-kun.

172
00:12:45,570 --> 00:12:50,740
You came up with the alliance idea
based on the things Hosen-kun said to you.

173
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:55,780
But it was all just bait to get you here.

174
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:58,250
Shut your damn mouth already.

175
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:03,540
If I take down Ayanokoji,
our class gets a huge deposit.

176
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:07,050
You know how far that'll put us ahead.

177
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:08,640
That's true.

178
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,160
But I haven't yet determined

179
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:16,770
if Ayanokoji-senpai is worthy
of being targeted that way!

180
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:19,770
You think I give a damn what you think?

181
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,340
If you're gonna try to stop me,
you can get the hell out!

182
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:25,280
Now...

183
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:31,160
Let's go, Ayanokoji!

184
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:44,800
You... Ayanokoji...

185
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:51,290
This knife—this petty knife—
is the one that I bought.

186
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:53,810
What're you talking about?

187
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:58,840
You'd lure us out here and
escalate things into a fight.

188
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:02,520
After seeing my classmates
hurt, I'd fly into a rage

189
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:06,650
and stab you with a knife
I happened to bring with me.

190
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:09,570
That's the sequence of events
you wanted to paint, right?

191
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:14,580
That's not how you hold a knife
when you want to stab someone else.

192
00:14:15,030 --> 00:14:19,330
You even turned the blade upside-down
so it would look like I stabbed you.

193
00:14:20,970 --> 00:14:26,590
And after figuring that out, you were
crazy enough to come let me stab you?

194
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:30,040
It was the best way to get you to stop.

195
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:32,520
Besides, you did the same thing.

196
00:14:32,930 --> 00:14:36,100
You expected to leave
this fight badly injured.

197
00:14:36,570 --> 00:14:41,100
It seems there's some kind
of special test in play here,

198
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:45,660
issued only to certain members
of the first-year class.

199
00:14:46,950 --> 00:14:48,840
And the object of that test...

200
00:14:49,230 --> 00:14:51,620
is to get me expelled.

201
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:57,160
How'd you know this was your knife?

202
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:00,200
I've done some investigating of my own.

203
00:15:00,610 --> 00:15:02,020
As of yesterday,

204
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:04,880
I was the only one who'd bought
a knife of this particular make.

205
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,940
What the hell?

206
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,130
Who the hell are you?!

207
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:10,170
What to do now, then?

208
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:14,640
Even if it is my knife,
you're the one who stabbed me.

209
00:15:14,890 --> 00:15:18,950
If you can't talk your way out of
this, you'll be expelled, Hosen.

210
00:15:19,950 --> 00:15:22,900
So you planned that part out, too...

211
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:26,660
Ayanokoji!

212
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,690
A-Are you all right?

213
00:15:29,070 --> 00:15:30,400
I'm fine.

214
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,660
How much did you know?

215
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:40,060
My suspicions first arose when I went
shopping at the mall with Amasawa.

216
00:15:40,650 --> 00:15:44,900
Amasawa-san? She's involved in this?

217
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:52,430
Yes. A clerk there saw another student
stop Hosen from buying the same knife.

218
00:15:53,050 --> 00:15:55,650
You're the one who thought
up the general plan,

219
00:15:56,010 --> 00:15:58,750
but Amasawa's the one who refined it.

220
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:04,100
She knew it would be best if the
knife used was one I'd bought myself.

221
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:07,040
And her coming to my apartment

222
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:10,820
to find her hair tie was a convenient
excuse to steal the knife.

223
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:12,720
She was careful not to get
her fingerprints on it

224
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,820
before giving it to you.

225
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:20,350
It was a damn mistake to work
with a woman I barely knew.

226
00:16:20,950 --> 00:16:25,830
No, Amasawa's the reason
your plan got this far.

227
00:16:26,650 --> 00:16:28,940
It would have fallen apart
much sooner without her.

228
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:35,090
Hosen, I'm willing to keep
this just between us.

229
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:37,600
The hell do you mean by that?

230
00:16:38,050 --> 00:16:42,390
In exchange, I have two requests.

231
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:48,360
One, I want the Class Ds to form
an alliance on equal footing.

232
00:16:48,830 --> 00:16:55,860
Two, I want you to be my partner
on the upcoming special test.

233
00:16:57,450 --> 00:17:00,940
Hosen is my ideal partner.

234
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:03,360
It's hard to imagine

235
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:06,760
a White Room student being willing
to attract so much attention.

236
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:12,340
Nice, nice work, Ayanokoji-senpai.

237
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:15,860
I've never gone toe-to-toe with
someone who excited me like this.

238
00:17:16,230 --> 00:17:20,350
I can see it wouldn't be any fun to
beat you into line with my fists.

239
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:24,050
I'll kill you sooner or later,
so look forward to that.

240
00:17:28,090 --> 00:17:34,970
The next Monday, Nanase and Horikita
negotiated an equal alliance,

241
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:37,060
and all partnerships were established.

242
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:40,030
We completed the special
test without issue,

243
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:43,790
and on May 1st,
the results were announced.

244
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Special Test  Results

245
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Math

246
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Class D

247
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Ayanokoji Kiyotaka

248
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Horikita Suzune

249
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Yukimura Teruhiko

250
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Wang Mei-yu

251
00:17:45,290 --> 00:17:47,790
Ishikura Kayoko

252
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:50,340
I won't make excuses.

253
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:52,050
As frustrating as it is,

254
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:57,800
I've been forced to acknowledge
your superiority twice in a row.

255
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,800
I admit defeat.

256
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:04,060
More importantly, regarding Nanase-san...

257
00:18:05,590 --> 00:18:10,330
So your friendly advances toward
us were all part of the act?

258
00:18:10,770 --> 00:18:15,080
I really did want to work
with you, Horikita-senpai.

259
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:16,070
However...

260
00:18:16,670 --> 00:18:21,320
The plan to take down Ayanokoji-senpai
was still the priority.

261
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:23,460
Why would you do that?

262
00:18:24,730 --> 00:18:27,610
"Ayanokoji Kiyotaka of Class 2-D."

263
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:30,960
"Any student responsible for expelling him

264
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:34,010
will be awarded
20 million private points."

265
00:18:34,590 --> 00:18:39,340
That is the special test we were given.

266
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:41,590
What the hell is that?

267
00:18:41,970 --> 00:18:46,600
Who issued such a ridiculous test?

268
00:18:49,150 --> 00:18:52,420
I've told you what you need to know.

269
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,730
Ayanokoji-senpai will know

270
00:18:54,730 --> 00:19:00,860
to be extremely cautious around
first-years aside from us.

271
00:19:01,550 --> 00:19:04,710
I'm going to need more than that from you!

272
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:05,870
You hurt Ayanokoji—

273
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:07,260
It's fine.

274
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:11,880
What she's told us about the
situation is more than enough.

275
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:17,380
Still, that's not the only
reason I helped Hosen-kun.

276
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:19,130
I also didn't believe

277
00:19:19,130 --> 00:19:24,390
that Ayanokoji-senpai was
worthy of this school.

278
00:19:25,290 --> 00:19:27,390
If what she said is true...

279
00:19:27,630 --> 00:19:31,050
There you are, Ayanokoji.

280
00:19:32,590 --> 00:19:34,230
I'll head back for now.

281
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:38,650
We'll speak another day about
our test score agreement.

282
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,400
How can I help you?

283
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:45,160
Acting Chairman Tsukishiro
wants to see you.

284
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:49,160
April has reached its end.

285
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:54,040
Have you figured out which is
the student who was sent here?

286
00:19:54,790 --> 00:19:55,850
Unfortunately not.

287
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:59,180
You admitted that very easily.

288
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:02,550
I don't want to make any
declarations unless I'm sure.

289
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,370
I see.

290
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:09,510
That means they've integrated very well.

291
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:14,680
I haven't sensed the unique
presence of a White Room student.

292
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:17,940
They've covered their scent completely.

293
00:20:18,230 --> 00:20:22,560
These last few months,
they've been put through a curriculum

294
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:25,450
to blend in perfectly with
high school students, I'm told.

295
00:20:25,930 --> 00:20:29,810
The fact that you couldn't
identify them at a glance...

296
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:33,960
I'll count that as a victory for now.

297
00:20:34,670 --> 00:20:36,570
You're free to leave now.

298
00:20:37,210 --> 00:20:40,310
Did you encounter unexpected
trouble with them?

299
00:20:40,970 --> 00:20:44,410
What makes you think that?

300
00:20:45,270 --> 00:20:48,720
You wanted the White Room
student to have me expelled,

301
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:52,020
but they didn't follow through.

302
00:20:52,650 --> 00:20:55,340
That's the only explanation
I can think of.

303
00:20:55,860 --> 00:21:00,480
That's certainly an interesting theory.

304
00:21:00,870 --> 00:21:03,780
Very well. I admit it.

305
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:09,370
The student in question ignored
the plan I laid out for them.

306
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:12,370
Be careful, Ayanokoji-kun.

307
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:16,620
The choice to bring the
White Room student here...

308
00:21:17,030 --> 00:21:19,000
was not my decision.

309
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:24,330
There's a chance the higher-ups
are plotting something.

310
00:21:26,260 --> 00:21:31,510
Tsukishiro and the White Room student
aren't a united front, then.

311
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:36,270
Or was that another lie to throw me off?

312
00:21:36,270 --> 00:21:42,950
And if that student is ignoring
even your father's directives,

313
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:47,930
a day may come when you wish
you had settled for expulsion.

314
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:54,100
The jealousy and hatred the
student feels toward you,

315
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:56,610
the White Room's masterpiece,
are unrelenting.

316
00:21:57,670 --> 00:22:01,670
What will they do to you
if left to their own devices?

317
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:05,390
I shudder just thinking about it.

318
00:22:06,190 --> 00:22:09,890
